        "summary":  "Three-quarters of CIOs regret major AI vendor or platform selections made in the past 18 months, with 29% reporting they have been asked to justify AI outcomes they could not fully interpret. The rapid pace of AI adoption has outpaced governance frameworks and best practices. Executives are pressuring IT leaders to deliver results with threats of budget cuts if targets are not met by mid-2026.",
        "execSummary":  "A three-quarters regret rate among CIOs on AI platform decisions is a critical warning for any leader currently evaluating or scaling AI investments ΓÇö speed without readiness produces expensive course corrections. The underlying pattern is consistent: vendor selection was driven by executive pressure and demo performance rather than integration readiness, total cost of ownership, and explainability requirements. For customer-support operations leaders, this is a direct caution against deploying AI agents before defining clear escalation logic, performance baselines, and governance accountability. The constructive takeaway is that a slower, more deliberate vendor evaluation process ΓÇö including outcome-based contracting ΓÇö significantly reduces regret risk.",
