        "summary":  "Unexpected AI expenses are forcing enterprises to reconsider their implementation strategies, with nearly half of organizations reporting that surprise costs have escalated to the board level. Poor visibility into spending across fragmented AI deployments spanning developer tools, infrastructure, and autonomous agents has prompted one-quarter of businesses to delay or cancel AI projects entirely. Experts recommend treating cost optimization as an architectural requirement and implementing stronger governance practices to prevent budgets from spiraling.",
