        "execSummary":  "The governance gap in enterprise AI is now quantified: 90% of companies fund governance programs but only 27% have mature ones ΓÇö and 86% are already testing AI agents without the policies to manage them. This combination is a compound risk, particularly in regulated industries where an AI incident without a documented response procedure creates direct liability. For senior leaders, the strategic priority is not to wait for governance frameworks to catch up ΓÇö it is to define minimum viable governance guardrails (escalation paths, audit logging, incident response playbooks) before expanding agent deployments. The Schellman data also signals that regulators will increasingly use governance maturity as an audit criterion, making this a compliance issue, not just an operational one.",
