        "summary":  "Tech companies including Microsoft, AWS, Google, OpenAI, and Anthropic are rapidly expanding forward deployed engineering programs to embed specialized engineers within enterprise customer organizations. These initiatives bridge the gap between AI technical capabilities and business needs as implementation complexity outpaces enterprise internal capacity. However, competition for skilled forward-deployed engineers is intense, and many organizations cannot sustain solutions long-term without ongoing vendor support.",
        "execSummary":  "Every major AI platform vendor is now investing billions to embed engineers directly inside enterprise customers ΓÇö a signal that self-service AI deployment has hit a complexity ceiling. This forward-deployed engineering model shifts AI implementation from a one-time project to an ongoing vendor relationship, with significant implications for enterprise negotiating leverage and total cost of ownership. For leaders scaling AI in customer-support or operations, this trend is a double-edged signal: access to deep technical expertise is available but creates long-term dependency on vendors for capabilities that should eventually be owned internally. The strategic counter-move is to treat FDE engagements as accelerated knowledge transfer programs, not permanent staffing solutions.",
