        "execSummary":  "As AI agents accelerate code generation and autonomous deployment, enterprises are introducing security blind spots faster than their governance frameworks can adapt. The core risk is not a dramatic AI failure but a gradual erosion of visibility and control over production systems ΓÇö a slow-moving crisis that security teams may not detect until a breach occurs. Leaders must treat AI governance as a non-negotiable prerequisite, not a post-deployment retrofit. The implication is clear: AI adoption timelines need to be paced against the maturity of security regression testing and access-control infrastructure.",
