        "summary":  "Matt Asay argues that AI should be deployed only for work tied to meaningful outcomes, not to generate unnecessary or impersonal output at scale. He warns against automating tasks simply because technology makes them cheaper, emphasizing that human judgment about what deserves to be created remains irreplaceable.",
