        "summary":  "The FCC has banned foreign-made humanoid and advanced robots from the US market, citing national security concerns about data collection and the need to protect the domestic robotics sector from Chinese competition. However, American research institutions rely heavily on affordable Chinese robots ΓÇö like the $4,600 Unitree models ΓÇö compared to $278,000 domestic alternatives, meaning the ban may hamper US AI research.",
